{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head f27f39581d707551b40b7dea303a664533059d00, artifact git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:f05500ed789f067cdb2ccdba9cb6988803c6d50d. Reviewed in a detached scratch worktree off that commit, one commit on top of main 77a38f6edead059ead93f03ff2b92fc0c19a551a, touching only .github/workflows/ci.yml (+2) and public_surface_test.go (+16/-1).\n\nFAILURE AND REPAIR. Reproduced the original break: cloned the head at depth 1 and ran the gate unchanged. It dies at the fixture push, \"! [remote rejected] f27f3958... -\u003e main (shallow update not allowed)\", and set -e aborts the script before the fixture exists. At the pinned actions/checkout 3d3c42e5 the fetch-depth default is 1, so CI was shallow; with fetch-depth \u003c= 0 that action takes the getRefSpecForAllHistory path, fetching +refs/heads/*:refs/remotes/origin/* and +refs/tags/*:refs/tags/* with no --depth, plus the pull-request merge ref on a pull_request event, so the candidate carries complete history under both trigger shapes. That is the faithful repair rather than symptom suppression: the alternative of receive.shallowUpdate on the fixture would leave a shallow origin whose clone is not what a public user gets, and the gate's whole claim is that the fixture models the first public push. The same gate on a genuine full clone pushed successfully and produced a fixture with sole refs/heads/main, checkout head exactly f27f3958, non-shallow, zero tags.\n\nMUTATIONS (focused test go test -run TestPublicRepositorySurface). Baseline green. fetch-depth: 0 -\u003e 1: RED, public_surface_test.go:87 'actions/checkout step does not contain \"fetch-depth: 0\"'. fetch-depth line removed entirely: RED, same message; removal reverts to the action default of 1, which is the broken state. fetch-depth: 0 moved into the setup-go step: RED, so the pin is scoped to the checkout step. persist-credentials: false -\u003e true: RED. persist-credentials line removed: RED. permissions contents: read -\u003e write: RED at line 71. Checkout moved to the last step with both settings dropped: RED for both, so the end-of-step slice does not run past the file into a false green. Deleting the sole-main assertion from verify-preview-clone.sh: RED. Unrelated edit (timeout-minutes 30 -\u003e 25): GREEN, so the pin is not over-broad.\n\nOUTPUT BOUNDARY, verified and mutated on the real fixture. The exact-refspec push yields exactly refs/heads/main and 2184 objects, identical to the object closure of the head; the clone has head exactly f27f3958, branch main, zero tags, zero refs/seq, and no extraheader or token in .git/config. Mutating the push to --mirror gives 95 refs and 8286 objects, --all gives 90 refs, main plus refs/seq/* gives 3 refs; the test \"$refs\" = \"refs/heads/main\" assertion fails on all three. The event log refs/seq/\u003cgenesis\u003e is a disjoint root history (root 5d262274) from main (root ec06411c) and is unreachable from the published head, so no envelope material can travel. Measured with the local gitleaks build: over all refs it reports 1768 generic-api-key findings in three commits, 1761 in checkpoint, 6 in attachments/discussion.json, 1 in event; none of those three commits is reachable from the head and none of those paths exists in its tree. Over the main-only fixture clone's whole history it reports no leaks found, 139 commits, 9.25 MB.\n\nSUPPLY CHAIN. All three actions are pinned to full commit SHAs, and git ls-remote confirms each SHA is exactly the commit its comment's tag points at upstream today: checkout v7.0.1, setup-go v7.0.0, setup-node v7.0.0. No moving tags anywhere in .github. permissions: contents: read sits at workflow level with no job-level override, and persist-credentials: false is a real setting because the action's own default is true.\n\nGATES at this head, all green: actionlint clean, make vet, make test 15/15 packages, make race 15/15, make build, npm test 49/49, make ui, make ui-check, make spike, git diff --exit-code, clean working tree, and verify-preview-clone.sh exit 0 with its fixture make test 15/15, vet and build. Tool versions actually invoked: /private/tmp/gitseq-public-tools-9f45a81/actionlint reports \"(devel), installed by building from source, built with go1.26.5\", not v1.7.12 as the ready-for-review report states; gitleaks from the same directory reports \"version is set by build process\". git 2.50.1, go 1.26.5.\n\nTHE CLONE GATE FAILED TWICE BEFORE IT PASSED, AND THE FAILURES WERE RUN DOWN. On the first two attempts this machine was at load average 31 and 25 with several concurrent agents. Attempt one failed TestWhoamiBoundsStallsAndRejectsRedirects at main_test.go:992, \"stalled resident was not bounded: elapsed=3.218220208s\". Attempt two failed the same test at 3.287915875s and also TestWarmDepth20000SummaryLatencyAndSize at view_test.go:344, \"warm depth-20k summary p99 = 844.771542ms, want \u003c 500ms\". Both assertions are wall-clock margins, a 3s bound on a 2s orientation timeout and a 500ms p99 bound; in the first the behaviour under test was correct and only the margin was exceeded (degraded=true). Re-run in isolation inside the same fixture checkout at load average 6, each passed 3 of 3, and a full clone-gate re-run at load average 5 passed with exit 0. Both tests also passed at this head in make test and make race. These are pre-existing load-sensitive latency assertions, unrelated to this diff, which touches no timeout, resident or statusview code. They deserve their own request; a hosted runner under noisy-neighbour load could hit them.\n\nNON-BLOCKING NOTES, none of which weakens what was previously reviewed. First, the step check anchors on the first \"uses: actions/checkout@\" only; a second job with an unprotected checkout passes both the test and actionlint. One job exists today. A comment carrying that anchor before the real step makes the test fail rather than pass, which is the safe direction. Second, the pins are substring matches, not YAML: commenting out either setting keeps the test and actionlint green. For fetch-depth the clone gate then fails loudly on its own, as reproduced; for persist-credentials there is no runtime backstop. This is the existing idiom of the file, and the change strictly strengthens persist-credentials by requiring it inside the checkout step rather than anywhere in the file. Third, the script's exact-head, branch-name and final cleanliness assertions are still not pinned by the surface test; pre-existing and untouched here. Fourth, at merge the live artifact for .github/workflows/ci.yml at 4d91ddaa needs superseding for the merge artifact to flare correctly.\n\nThe head did not move at any point during this review.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:f05500ed789f067cdb2ccdba9cb6988803c6d50d","head":"f27f39581d707551b40b7dea303a664533059d00","verdict":"approved"}}